WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
The archive publishes a scanned map under an
immutable versioned URL.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:11.448
If 2,000 eligible map requests arrive per second and
edge caches serve 92 percent as fresh hits, a

00:00:11.448 --> 00:00:15.972
simplified model sends about 160 fetches per second
toward origin.

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:22.690
This estimate excludes validation and other traffic,
but it shows the source of the benefit: saved

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.569
content answers repeated reads near users.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.544
A private account page is a different object and
cannot safely share the same reuse policy.

00:00:31.544 --> 00:00:37.553
Anycast answers a different question: which network
location receives traffic for an address

00:00:37.553 --> 00:00:39.512
advertised from several sites?

00:00:39.512 --> 00:00:45.848
Routing chooses a path using network policy and
topology, not a guarantee of geographic nearness.

00:00:45.848 --> 00:00:49.517
A CDN can use anycast, DNS steering and caching
together.

00:00:49.517 --> 00:00:55.568
Cache directives still determine whether an answer
may be reused, and route changes still need

00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:57.950
handling for established connections.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:04.129
A private directive excludes shared-cache storage of
the whole response; a long max-age does not

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:04.902
override it.

00:01:04.902 --> 00:01:10.953
Distinguish traffic steering, content reuse and
application correctness when reviewing an edge

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:11.403
design.

00:01:11.448 --> 00:01:16.490
Design an archive service for the morning a newly
digitized collection opens.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:22.908
Public scans can use versioned URLs and edge
caching, while requests to reserve the last
available

00:01:22.908 --> 00:01:27.754
research-room seat must reach application logic and
authoritative storage.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:32.601
Draw DNS discovery, the edge, a regional entry
point, workers and storage.

00:01:32.648 --> 00:01:38.369
Label where a read may be answered without
contacting origin and where a write must be checked

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:39.708
against current state.

00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:44.151
Now fail one worker during the surge and one region
during a reservation.

00:01:44.151 --> 00:01:50.055
Explain the delay before health information changes,
what happens to in-flight requests and which

00:01:50.055 --> 00:01:52.672
clients might still use cached DNS answers.

00:01:52.672 --> 00:01:59.271
A retry must not create two reservations, and a
second worker must not allocate the same final seat

00:01:59.271 --> 00:02:00.138
concurrently.

00:02:00.138 --> 00:02:06.537
Those requirements need an explicit data and
operation contract, not just another load balancer.

00:02:06.537 --> 00:02:13.070
A convincing design combines routing, capacity,
freshness and recovery assumptions, then tests the

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.603
failure cases that could violate them.
